            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>Cumberland Heritage Village Museum is a recreated 1920s and 30s village offering a vintage rural setting just 30 minutes from downtown Ottawa. With dozens of historic and true-to-era buildings, acres of greenspace, and gardens, the Museum provides a nostalgic backdrop for your special occasion.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Use the&nbsp;<a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/recreation-and-parks/facilities/facility-rentals">rental search tool</a>&nbsp;to find an event space that meets your needs.&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/recreation-and-parks/facilities/facility-rentals/community-hall-cumberland-heritage-village-museum">Community Hall</a></li>
<li><a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/recreation-and-parks/facilities/facility-rentals/church-cumberland-heritage-village-museum">Knox Church</a></li>
<li><a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/recreation-and-parks/facilities/facility-rentals/gazebo-picnic-shelter-and-tent-trio-cumberland-heritage-village-museum">Gazebo, picnic shelter and tent (Trio)</a></li>
</ul>
<p>For more information, please contact our Customer Service Booking Clerk. Call <strong>613-580-2988</strong>&nbsp;or email <a href="mailto:museecumberlandmuseum@ottawa.ca">museecumberlandmuseum@ottawa.ca</a>.</p>
